.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- set up the downtime logger virtual environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstrap.sh
.RB [ \-\-dev ]
.RB [ \-\-postgres ]
.RB [ \-\-recreate ]
.br
.B bootstrap.sh
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page documents the
.B bootstrap.sh
at the top of the
.B mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger
checkout.
The script changes to its own directory, creates
.I venv/
with
.B $PYTHON \-m venv
if it does not exist, activates it, upgrades
.BR pip ,
.B setuptools
and
.BR wheel ,
and then:
.IP 1. 4
if a sibling checkout
.I ../mu2edaq\-discovery
exists, installs it editable
.RB ( "pip install \-\-upgrade \-e ../mu2edaq\-discovery" ),
which enables service\-discovery announcements;
.IP 2. 4
installs this package editable
.RB ( "pip install \-\-upgrade \-e ." ),
with the extras selected by the options.
.PP
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
is not on PyPI and is deliberately not a declared dependency; without the
sibling checkout the application runs with discovery off.
.PP
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1)
runs this script automatically when
.I venv/bin/activate
is missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Add the
.B dev
extra
.RB ( pytest ,
.BR pytest\-qt ).
.TP
.B \-\-postgres
Add the
.B postgres
extra
.RB ( psycopg2\-binary ).
The shipped storage backend is SQLite only; this provides the driver for a
user\-written PostgreSQL backend.
.TP
.B \-\-recreate
Delete
.I venv/
and build it again.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment.
.TP
.I pyproject.toml
Dependency declaration used by the editable install.
.TP
.I ../mu2edaq\-discovery
Optional sibling checkout installed first when present.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Interpreter used to create the environment.
Default
.BR python3 .
The package declares
.B requires\-python >= 3.9
(AlmaLinux 9 system Python).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The environment is ready.
.TP
.B 1
Unknown option.
.TP
.B >0
A failing
.B python
or
.B pip
step; the script runs under
.B set \-e
and exits with that step's status.
.SH EXAMPLES
First\-time setup with the test tools:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh \-\-dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rebuild from scratch with a specific interpreter:
.PP
.RS
.nf
PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3.9 ./bootstrap.sh \-\-recreate
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1)
